menu "sys_system"

    config SYS_SYSTEM_DEADMAN_DEFAULT_MS
        int "Dead-man timeout at boot (ms, 0 = off)"
        default 0
        range 0 60000
        help
          0, or the dead-man's time (150..60000) of the sessions app/runit
          attaches at boot (the console and the runIT BLE pair), with the
          safety flag: their end enters the safe state. Changed per session at runtime with the sys
          DEADMAN command; not stored.

    config SYS_SYSTEM_TIME_PERIOD_S
        int "Time broadcast period (s)"
        default 60
        range 5 3600
        help
          A board sends its time on every open session this often (and when a
          client sets it, and when a peer is reached), so the clocks of the
          boards that talk follow it.

endmenu
